# Dottie research loop — continuous, hill-climbing automated research.
# Install on your box with:  crontab apps/dottie/research_orchestration/crontab
# Edit DOTTIE_ROOT to your checkout, and set Ollama env if not on defaults.
#
# flock (inside research_worker.sh) guarantees single-instance per worker: if a 14-hour training
# run is still going, the next hourly training tick is silently skipped instead of stacking.
#
# Cadence mirrors the closed-loop architecture: ideation daily (establishes the frontier),
# implement/train/evaluate hourly and staggered so each stage feeds the next.

DOTTIE_ROOT=/home/user/workspace/dottie
DOTTIE_OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
DOTTIE_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3:32b
SHELL=/bin/bash

# 1. Ideation — daily at midnight. Grounds N hypotheses in the current real baseline + dead ends.
# 0  0 * * *  $DOTTIE_ROOT/apps/dottie/research_orchestration/research_worker.sh ideate --n 3 --bottleneck "early pre-training loss spikes and MoE routing collapse"

# 2. Implementation — minute 15 hourly. Drafts + 4-level-validates the next pending hypothesis.
# 15 * * * *  $DOTTIE_ROOT/apps/dottie/research_orchestration/research_worker.sh implement

# 3. Training — minute 30 hourly. Real measurement; flock skips the tick if a run is in flight.
# 30 * * * *  $DOTTIE_ROOT/apps/dottie/research_orchestration/research_worker.sh train --steps 200

# 4. Evaluation & hill-climb — minute 45 hourly. Promotes only on a real, paired improvement.
# 45 * * * *  $DOTTIE_ROOT/apps/dottie/research_orchestration/research_worker.sh evaluate

# Continuous runner (replaces the per-stage cadence above, kept commented for
# reference): chains evaluate->train->implement->ideate immediately; the hourly
# flock line is a self-heal heartbeat — a live runner makes it a no-op.
5 * * * *  $DOTTIE_ROOT/apps/dottie/research_orchestration/research_worker.sh run --trainer factory --steps 150 --max-retries 5 --n 3
